{{also|kartoffel}}
==German==
{{wikipedia|lang=de}}

===Etymology===
From older {{m|de|Tartuffel}} or {{m|de|Tartüffel}}, from {{der|de|it|tartufolo||truffle}}, from {{der|de|ML.|*territūberum}} or {{der|de|la|[[terrae]] [[tuber]]}}.

The use as an ethnic nickname is due to the prominence of potatoes in German cuisine, particularly vis-à-vis the cuisines of the major immigrant communities in the country. (Compare the corresponding {{m|de|Spaghetti}} used to refer to Italians.)

